EdgeFDL is written in Python. The source code, the Web dashboard (edgefdl/core/web/index.html,
which loads no third-party scripts, stylesheets or fonts), the demo topology and sample device
configurations in configs/, the released model bundle and results in results/, and the figures and
screenshots in docs/ are original work of the EdgeFDL contributors. No third-party source code is
bundled, adapted or vendored. Two texts in the repository come from elsewhere: LICENSE is the
Apache License 2.0 published by the Apache Software Foundation, and CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is the
Contributor Covenant 2.1 (https://www.contributor-covenant.org, CC BY 4.0), attributed in the file.

The components below are not contained in this repository. They are installed by the user and keep
their own licenses.


Python packages imported at run time (installed with pip from requirements.txt)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NumPy (>= 1.19)                   BSD-3-Clause
PyTorch (>= 2.0; CPU build is     BSD-3-Clause
  sufficient)
PyYAML (>= 5.3)                   MIT
psutil (>= 5.7), optional         BSD-3-Clause
                                      Used only for the process CPU and memory figures shown by the
                                      dashboard and /api/status and measured by `python -m edgefdl
                                      bench`; EdgeFDL runs without it.

The published results were produced with Python 3.13 and PyTorch 2.9.1 (a CUDA 12.8 build, run
on the CPU). The HTTP server, REST API, Syslog and Webhook sinks use only the Python standard
library.


External programs invoked as separate processes (not linked, not distributed)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The `netns` and `lxd` backends of the equivalent virtual network, and the real-stack lab container,
run the following programs through their command-line interfaces. EdgeFDL neither links against
them nor includes any of their code, and does not distribute them; they are installed from the
operating system's packages. The `sim` backend, training, evaluation and the dashboard in simulation
mode run none of them.

FRRouting (zebra, ospfd, vtysh)   GPL-2.0-or-later
iproute2 (ip, tc)                 GPL-2.0
iputils (ping)                    BSD-3-Clause for ping; the iputils package also contains tools
                                      under GPL-2.0-or-later
traceroute                        GPL-2.0
iperf3                            BSD-3-Clause
procps (sysctl)                   GPL-2.0-or-later
LXD (lxc command-line client)     AGPL-3.0-only since LXD 5.20 (Apache-2.0 up to LXD 5.19);
                                      the LXD client SDKs remain Apache-2.0. Run as a separate
                                      program by the `lxd` backend only.


Development and test environment (not part of EdgeFDL, not distributed)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/lab/Dockerfile describes a local test image that `scripts/lab.sh build` builds on the
user's machine from the Debian 12 base image (debian:bookworm-slim) and Debian packages (frr,
iperf3, traceroute, iproute2, iputils-ping, procps, python3, python3-yaml, python3-numpy,
ca-certificates). Each package keeps its own license as recorded by Debian. No image is published
or distributed by the EdgeFDL project. Docker itself is used only to build and run this image.
